    "arab48EN": "According to the official anabin database, the Bagrut certificate grants direct university admission for all subjects at all universities, provided the matriculation exams include Mathematics at 3 units, English at 4 units, and one additional subject at 4 units. There is no official GPA threshold (such as 65 or 75) for direct admission, but the converted grade matters for admission-restricted (NC) programmes. Applicants who do not meet these subject conditions can qualify via a Studienkolleg (T-Kurs for engineering) and the Feststellungsprüfung exam. Many universities process international applications via uni-assist.de, while some require direct application — always check the university website."
