    "arab48EN": "Senior accounting professions are regulated in Germany: Steuerberater (tax advisor) requires 2-3 years of practice plus a state exam; Wirtschaftsprüfer (auditor) requires 3-4 years of auditing practice plus the WP exam. The German tax and financial system differs from the Israeli one. According to the official anabin database, the Bagrut certificate grants direct university admission for all subjects at all universities, provided the matriculation exams include Mathematics at 3 units, English at 4 units, and one additional subject at 4 units. There is no official GPA threshold for direct admission, but the converted grade matters for admission-restricted (NC) programs. Many universities process international applications via uni-assist.de, while some require direct application — always check the university's website and apply early."
